# wiki-mixin: begin v1.1
#
# v1.1 (2026-09-14) supersedes v1.0. If a repo's block still says v1.0, its
# policy is unknown rather than old: three different policies shipped under that
# one version string, so the marker could not answer "is this repo patched?".
# `~/.claude/scripts/wiki-raw-audit.sh` answers it by inspection instead.
#
# WHY THIS BLOCK EXISTS
#
# wiki/raw holds incoming client mail verbatim, written by an automated ingest.
# Tracking it keeps every wiki page's cited source resolvable in a fresh clone,
# which is genuinely useful. It also means anything a client mails us is
# committed and pushed without a human in the loop.
#
# Twice that went wrong through the same mechanism:
#   2026-08-25  a client's plaintext MSSQL password, mailed to us, swept into a
#               pushed branch by a broad `git add`.
#   2026-08-17  ten operative reports with patient name, date of service and
#               procedure IN THE FILENAME, auto-committed and pushed to a vendor
#               we hold no BAA with. Found 24 days later.
#
# v1.0 excluded mp4/mov/zip — chosen for repository SIZE, and silent about the
# formats clinical and contractual documents actually arrive in. That silence is
# the gap.
#
# THE RULE: message bodies are tracked, attachments are not.
#
# A body is text, it is what a wiki page cites, and it is what the PHI screen
# can read. An attachment is an opaque payload whose filename alone can disclose.
# The cost is that a fresh clone cannot open an attachment a page cites — the
# right trade against putting client documents in a vendor's storage.

# Size (v1.0, retained)
wiki/raw/**/*.mp4
wiki/raw/**/*.mov
wiki/raw/**/*.mp3
wiki/raw/**/*.zip

# Documents. The 2026-09-10 rule, now the default everywhere rather than a
# patch applied to one repo during an incident.
wiki/raw/**/*.pdf
wiki/raw/**/*.doc
wiki/raw/**/*.docx
wiki/raw/**/*.xls
wiki/raw/**/*.xlsx
wiki/raw/**/*.xlsb
wiki/raw/**/*.ppt
wiki/raw/**/*.pptx
wiki/raw/**/*.rtf
wiki/raw/**/*.dat

# Images: a screenshot of a record is a record.
wiki/raw/**/*.jpg
wiki/raw/**/*.jpeg
wiki/raw/**/*.png
wiki/raw/**/*.gif
wiki/raw/**/*.tif
wiki/raw/**/*.tiff

# Whole mail objects carry their own attachments inside them.
wiki/raw/**/*.eml
wiki/raw/**/*.msg

# For a repo that should not track raw at all — a public repo, or any bundle
# whose sources are reproducible elsewhere — uncomment this instead of the above.
# It is the safer default and two repos already use it.
# wiki/raw/
# wiki-mixin: end
